@startuml
title Optional LLM Data Boundary

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Incident operator" as Operator
database "Confidential kdiag collection\nraw node and Kubernetes evidence" as Collection
component "kdiag LLM preparation\nbounded fragments, pseudonymization, DLP" as Kdiag
folder "Local incident package\nidentifiers retained" as LocalPackage
folder "External export\nincident, prompt, preview, manifest" as ExternalExport
folder "Private mapping\nmode 0600" as TokenMap
cloud "Separate local inference service\nno cluster credentials or tools" as LocalLLM
cloud "Google AI Search\nmanual operation only" as Google

Operator --> Kdiag : prepare and validate
Kdiag --> Collection : resolve selected evidence references
Kdiag --> LocalPackage : IDs plus bounded evidence fragments
LocalPackage ..> LocalLLM : loopback HTTP content transfer
Kdiag --> ExternalExport : pseudonymized fragments after DLP
Kdiag --> TokenMap : original values stay local
Operator --> ExternalExport : review every exported file
Operator --> Google : manually copy reviewed export
Google --> Operator : manually save untrusted response
Operator --> Kdiag : import response
Kdiag --> TokenMap : restore known tokens only

TokenMap -[hidden]-> Google
note on link
  Forbidden transfer
end note
@enduml
